implementationPlan.description:
Single verification gate, run fresh after steps 1-2:
`cd packages/moe-daemon && npx vitest run src/tools/submitPlan.test.ts src/server/McpAdapter.test.ts src/util/rails.test.ts src/state/executionContract.test.ts`
It must exit 0. Its command, exitCode and outputTail are the complete_task verification.

The narrow scope is deliberate:
- this task changes no production code;
- these four suites pin the handler, the adapter serialization, the rails matcher and the contract scan that the docs now describe;
- CQ-F12 owns the epic's full regression.

In WSL, run from a native-Linux snapshot (mem gotcha-linux-vitest-reuse-native-node-modules, mem gotcha-daemon-tests-ambient-moe-worker-id):
- git archive HEAD;
- overlay this task's three files and cmp them against the worktree;
- symlink a native Linux node_modules;
- use a Linux-only PATH with MOE_* scrubbed.
Never npm install over the shared Windows node_modules. Record the snapshot's HEAD sha.
Report any failure honestly, by name: no skip, no weakening. affectedFiles is empty on purpose.
